le only to logged-in residents via the Next.js frontend. |\\\\n| **Resident Directory**       | Opt-in list of residents                                | Custom boolean field ('Show in Directory') will be added to Strapi's User model. The 'My Profile' page in Next.js will allow users to edit this preference. The directory page will only fetch and display users who have opted in. |\\\\n| **Contact Form**             | Contact Us Page                                         | A standard form in Next.js will send data to a custom Strapi API endpoint. The submission will be saved to a 'Contact Message' Collection Type in the PostgreSQL database for admin review. |\\\\n\\\\n**4. High-Level Workflows**\\\\n\\\\n*   **Content Administration:** The HOA Administrator will log into the dedicated Strapi Admin UI (e.g., `admin.hoa-website.com`) to manage all site content without needing any technical knowledge.\\\\n*   **Resident Experience:** Residents will visit the main website (e.g., `www.hoa-website.com`), log in to access their dashboard and private resources, all served by the Next.js application.\\\\n*   **Public Experience:** Prospective buyers and the public will browse the high-performance static pages of the main website.\\\\n\\\\n**5. Conclusion and Next Steps**\\\\n\\\\nThis unified plan confirms that the proposed technical architecture fully supports the required product features. The headless approach provides an optimal blend of user-friendliness for administrators and a modern, secure experience for residents.\\\\n\\\\nThis is a preliminary plan. The next critical step is for the newly assembled technical team to perform a more detailed analysis, which will lead to the creation of detailed data models, API contracts, and a full task breakdown for the final DEP.\\\\n\\\\nWe are confident in this strategic direction and await further orders.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04\\\"\\n}\\n###VANTO-GIDEON-REPORT-20250629-01###\"}],\"role\"